# Provider Adapters

Interfaces describe MintReels needs. They must not mirror a vendor’s raw API.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — PyAI-shaped interface
transcribePyAIHear(req: PyAIHearRequest): Promise<PyAIHearResponse>

// ✅ GOOD — product-shaped interface
transcribe(input: TranscriptionInput): Promise<Transcript>
```

## Defaults

```env
AI_PROVIDER=pyai
KNOWLEDGE_BASE_PROVIDER=pyai
STORAGE_PROVIDER=filestack
QUEUE_PROVIDER=bullmq
EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=openai
VECTOR_STORE_PROVIDER=qdrant
```

## Placement

- AI interfaces: `packages/ai/src/{speech,llm,embedding,vector-store}-provider.ts`
- PyAI AI: `packages/ai/src/providers/pyai/`
- OpenAI-compatible LLM/embeddings: `packages/ai/src/providers/openai-compatible/`
- Qdrant vector store: `packages/ai/src/providers/qdrant/` (vendor types stay inside the adapter)
- KB interface: `packages/knowledge/src/provider.ts`
- PyAI KB: `packages/knowledge/src/adapters/pyai/` (mapper keeps vendor types inside)
- Storage: `packages/storage/src/provider.ts` + `filestack.ts` (Filestack REST; HMAC policy only if `FILESTACK_APP_SECRET` is set)
- Queue: `packages/queue/src/provider.ts` + `bullmq.ts`

## Provider-neutral hook logic

Dedup, diversity ranking, and clip boundaries are product logic, not adapters. They live in
`packages/ai/src/hook-selection.ts` and `packages/ai/src/clip-boundaries.ts` as pure functions and
depend only on `VectorStoreProvider` / `EmbeddingProvider` — never on Qdrant/OpenAI types.

`VectorStoreProvider` exposes `fetch(ids)` so downstream steps reuse embeddings already in the index
instead of re-embedding (cost control). MySQL stays canonical; the index is rebuildable.

## Do not

- Add a local / pgvector Knowledge Base adapter.
- Store embeddings in MySQL.
- Call vendor SDKs from apps or `packages/domain`.
